- On resolution failure, switches error context to the discovered subcommand, optionally prints the error and help hint, then returns (`command.go:1095–1106`).
- Marks the command as called, records its invoked name, propagates the root context when needed, and invokes `cmd.execute(flags)` (`command.go:1108–1116`).

